# Line endings are stated rather than inherited from whoever clones this.
#
# The plugin only runs on Windows, where either ending works - PowerShell 5.1 parses
# LF files and the C# compiler does not care - but "either works" is the assumption
# that produces a diff of every file the moment somebody with a different
# core.autocrlf touches the repository. Saying it here makes a checkout byte-identical
# for everyone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native sources, kept in the ending their tooling has always seen.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cs text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Images and the compiled helper cache are bytes, not lines.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.svg binary
